---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import PlaceholderBox from "../components/PlaceholderBox.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import { SITE, href } from "../site.config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Field work"
  description="Workshops and site visits at HBRI and NARC, Islamabad, as stated by the team. Photos to be added."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Field work"
    intro="Workshops and site visits at the Honeybee Research Institute (HBRI) and the National Agricultural Research Centre (NARC), Islamabad — as stated by the team. Photos to be added."
  >
    <p><StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Photos to be added" /></p>
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="container">
    <h2>What the team states</h2>
    <p>
      The team states that workshops and site visits took place at HBRI and NARC, Islamabad. Dates,
      photos, and written confirmations have not yet been supplied. Until they are, this page uses
      cautious wording only: workshops and site visits. It does not claim that the system was tested
      in the field, that experts endorsed it, or that any result was confirmed there.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing is published here about what experts said or what was checked during those visits,
      because the team has not supplied that material.
    </p>
    <PlaceholderBox text="visit dates, photos with permissions, and written confirmations from HBRI and NARC" />
    <figure>
      <img src={href("/images/stock/beehive_apiary.jpg")} alt="Beehives in an apiary" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>
        Illustrative image. Beehives in an apiary. This is a stock photo, not a photo of the
        team's field work. Credits:
        <a href={href("/credits")}>Image credits</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>The institutions</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Honeybee Research Institute (HBRI)</strong> is an institute of the
      <strong>National Agricultural Research Centre (NARC)</strong>, Islamabad, under the Pakistan
      Agricultural Research Council (PARC). These official names and the "Centre" spelling follow
      PARC's own publications. The abbreviation HBRC belongs to a different centre abroad and is
      not used here.
    </p>
    <p>
      Source (PARC):
      <a href={SITE.links.parcHbriNews} rel="noopener">PARC news: Bee Hive Products Laboratory at HBRI, NARC</a> ·
      PARC website: <a href={SITE.links.parc} rel="noopener">parc.gov.pk</a>
    </p>

    <h2>What the project report says</h2>
    <p>
      The project report does not mention HBRI, NARC, Islamabad, workshops, or site visits. Its own
      limits section states that testing stayed mainly in laboratory and controlled settings, and
      that performance in working apiaries over full seasons was largely untested (§6.3.3, §6.5.1).
      The small expert checks described in the report involved a small number of beekeepers and a
      small set of images from one unnamed local operation (§11.8). No names, dates, or places are
      given for those checks, and none are published here.
    </p>
    <p>
      The workshops and site visits described above are therefore presented as team statements from
      outside the report, not as report findings. If evidence shows they happened after the report
      was written, dates on the <a href={href("/journey")}>Journey</a> page will say so.
    </p>

    <h2>Photos and permissions</h2>
    <PlaceholderBox text="field photos and videos, with consent from every person pictured and permission from each institution" />
    <p>
      No field photos are shown. No institute name, logo, or statement is used as an endorsement.
      Institutional permission is required before any such use. See
      <a href={href("/research")}>Research</a> for what the report itself supports.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
